<!--
  EN: app_font_face_scene.rml -- fixture for tests/app_font_face_sanity.cpp (UI-FONTFACE,
      App-path forward-coverage gate). Same shape as tests/fontface_scene.rml (the UiLayer-path
      fixture): NO `@font-face` block -- every family this scene ever renders with is registered
      PROGRAMMATICALLY, via glintfx::App::load_font_face(), which is the exact call this fixture
      exists to exercise. "#txt" is `display: inline-block`, zero padding/border/margin,
      `white-space: nowrap` -- same get_element_box()-oracle convention every other fonteng_*
      scene in this suite uses. `font-family`/text content are set dynamically per probe via
      App::set_property(id, "font-family", ...) / App::set_text(id, ...).
  PT: app_font_face_scene.rml -- fixture pra tests/app_font_face_sanity.cpp (UI-FONTFACE, gate de
      cobertura de forward do caminho App). Mesmo formato de tests/fontface_scene.rml (a fixture
      do caminho UiLayer): SEM bloco `@font-face` -- toda família que esta cena algum dia
      renderiza é registrada PROGRAMATICAMENTE, via glintfx::App::load_font_face(), que é
      exatamente a chamada que esta fixture existe pra exercitar. "#txt" é
      `display: inline-block`, padding/borda/margem zero, `white-space: nowrap` -- mesma
      convenção de oráculo via get_element_box() que todo outro fonteng_* desta suíte usa.
      `font-family`/conteúdo de texto são definidos dinamicamente por sonda via
      App::set_property(id, "font-family", ...) / App::set_text(id, ...).
-->
<rml>
<head>
  <title>app_font_face_sanity</title>
  <style>
    body {
      background-color: #000000;
      width: 100%;
      height: 100%;
      margin: 0;
    }
    #txt {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: 0;
      margin: 0;
      white-space: nowrap;
      position: absolute;
      left: 20px;
      top: 20px;
      font-size: 40px;
      color: #ffffff;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div id="txt"></div>
</body>
</rml>
